==English==

===Etymology===
Recorded c. 1600, perhaps from the interpretation of {{m|en|tilt||a joust}} as derived from "leaning" into an attack, presumably a folk etymology, as {{m|en|tilt}} in late Middle English meant “a covering of coarse cloth, an awning” and referred to the barrier separating the combatants in a joust.

